{
  "page_dict": {
    "alltext": "36.\n44 INT. PUB-BAR TABLE - NIGHT\nVEDA is sitting at the bar counter, holding a glass of beer.\nThere are empty bottles lying next to the PUG. The PUG puts\nhis paw into the glass and licks it, lies down again and\nbarks.\nVEDA\nChaalivaaltiki... naa kanna ekkuva\nthaagava?\nThe PUG barks again\nVEDA\nNormuye. Beer bottleantha levu.\nPosthe peepa lepesettattunnaavu...\nThe PUG looks at him with his big brown eyes and then turns\nhis head away.\nVEDA\nabbo....alaaka, neeku thindi\npettadame ekkuva. Mandhu kuda\nadiginantha poyaalaa..dishti\npettakunda gammuna paduko.\nVEDA leans and whispers in the PUG’s ear\nVEDA\nArdham chesukove........naa\ndhaggarinka dabbulu levu. Unnaa ee\nkaastha neeke posthe ela cheppu.\nNeni konchem thaagesthanu.\nChakkagaa intikelli podaam.\nThe PUG barks at him and moves a few feet away and lies on\nthe bar counter.\nVEDA\nChee...... nuvvu kukka jaathike\nkalamkame, assalu vishvaasam\nledu...Idhigo thaagu\nSULOCHANA who has been watching of all of this, comes\ncharging at VEDA.\nSULOCHANA\nManishiva pasuvvaa?.. Evadanna\nkukkapilla ki mandhu posthaara??..\nAdi antha glassa... chasthe?\nVEDA looks at her wondering why she is bothered. They\nsuddenly see each other properly.",
